---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const pageTitle = "Karina";
---
<Layout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
    <div class="gif">
        <img src="/images/space.webp" alt="Space background" role="presentation" width="300" height="259" decoding="async">
    </div>
    <h1>Karina</h1>
    <span class="badge">Data Engineer</span>
    <h2>About</h2>
    <p>
        What really pulled me into data engineering is that hidden stretch of work nobody sees from the outside.
    </p>
    <p>
        There’s this gap between “okay, the data is in the database” and “the number on the dashboard is actually correct”
        — and in that gap sit a bunch of small decisions: how you lay out the files, where you do the aggregations, how you check that everything
        still makes sense. Any one of those choices can either keep the reports solid or completely wreck them, and then you’re stuck digging for
        a week trying to figure out what went wrong.
    </p>
    <p>
        I like building the layers so you can tear the whole pipeline down and put it back together
        from zero, check it, and still be able to explain exactly where every single number came from.
    </p>
    <p>
        I work with Python, PostgreSQL, ClickHouse,
        dbt, Airflow, and S3-compatible storage. And yeah, I actually read the docs and the library source code myself — half the answers are
        sitting right there.
    </p>

    <div class="center">
        <a href="/works/">
            <button class="btn">My portfolio</button>
        </a>
    </div>
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <div class="skills center">
        <!-- Python -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="Python"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/python/python-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">Python</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Pandas -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="Pandas"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/pandas/pandas-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">Pandas</span>
        </div>

        <!-- PostgreSQL -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="PostgreSQL"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/postgresql/postgresql-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">PostgreSQL</span>
        </div>

        <!-- MySQL -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="MySQL"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/mysql/mysql-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">MySQL</span>
        </div>

        <!-- ClickHouse -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="ClickHouse"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/clickhouse/clickhouse-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">ClickHouse</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Apache Airflow -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="Apache Airflow"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/apacheairflow/apacheairflow-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">Airflow</span>
        </div>

        <!-- dbt -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="dbt"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/simple-icons@v13/icons/dbt.svg"
                 style="filter: invert(1) brightness(1.2);"/>
            <span class="skill-name">dbt</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Apache Spark -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="Apache Spark"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/devicons/devicon@latest/icons/apachespark/apachespark-original.svg"/>
            <span class="skill-name">Spark</span>
        </div>

        <!-- MinIO -->
        <div class="skill-item">
            <img class="skills__img" width="46" height="46" alt="MinIO"
                 src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/simple-icons@v13/icons/minio.svg"
                 style="filter: invert(1) brightness(1.2);"/>
            <span class="skill-name">MinIO</span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <h2>Interests</h2>
    <p>
        Of all the ways I can spend an evening, I most often choose the one where I get to figure out why people are the way they are.
    </p>
    <p>
        I read popular science — mostly sociology, theology and feminist theory — and what I love most are the places
        where these views refuse to agree with each other: how religion pulls people into a community and how it also
        keeps that community tightly controlled, who decided what counts as normal and when, why some explanations of
        the world last for centuries while others fall apart in ten years.
    </p>
    <p>
        I like that these books never hand you the right answer at the end. They just give you a more honest version of the question.
    </p>
    <p>
        I love foreign languages. For me a language is more of an access key than a skill — every vocabulary carries a way
        of talking about the world that simply doesn’t occur to you in your native tongue.
    </p>
    <p>
        Sport is the opposite story: there I don’t optimise anything. Just two hours with the phone left in the locker,
        and somehow afterwards thinking becomes easier.
    </p>
</Layout>


